recommendations.text:
Capital allocation, our reserved matter (inference: our record holds no reinstatement).

Net debt has been at the historical level since 2029 (2030 under stress), and stress free cash flow is about $17.2B in 2050. We are minded to take up the Round 3 proposal in this form:
- reinstate a common dividend of about $3B a year first;
- add a buyback of $0-5B a year, authorised by this Board each year on Finance Committee review and paced on actual free cash flow;
- cap the two together at $8B a year, about 46% of 2050 stress free cash flow and 37% of base, well short of the pre-2019 practice of returning about all free cash flow.

Conditions:
- net debt at or below zero in the stress case;
- revolvers undrawn and no new equity;
- supplier funding first;
- the buyback goes to zero first on any live problem;
- the agencies' confirmation that the rating is solidly investment grade, not management's inference.

Nothing is announced before we decide.

