(3) McCabe's co-signature on any launch, with her worst column, capex a year and funding. In every case, also her quarterly report:
- narrowbody ramp and early-unit costs against her base of about $1.9-4.3B and worst case of about $7.5B ($9B if we carry a retrofit alone);
- the net LTSA balance;
- a statement that no balance-sheet trigger stands.

(4) Watson's report to the Safety, Energy Transition & Tech Committee:
- in-service durability on NGSA (since 2037) and fps (since 2040);
- life-limited parts at full life;
